{
  "title": "Calorie architecture phase 2: fill missing weights into the catalog offline and delete the runtime weights queue",
  "description": "Phase 2 of the design in doc/calorie-estimates.md (\"Architecture\"), approved 2026-10-11: calories for a known food should be a pure lookup with no LLM calls or queues. \
Today a second runtime queue (server/src/ingredient_weights.rs, table ingredient_weight_estimates) asks the LLM for grams per cup or per piece when the catalog lacks them, queued by the estimate-calories read path, and is shown in the weights half of Settings -> Ingredient recognition. \
Replace it: add a dev-time command (for example make catalog-fill-weights, reusing ramekin-core/src/ai/estimate_ingredient_weights.rs) that collects the weight gaps across the pipeline fixtures and snapshots (cli/src/ingredient_catalog_audit.rs already counts them, \"Weights to estimate\"), asks once, and writes them into the catalog (curated.json portions or grams_per_cup) with a citation naming the model. \
The values are reviewed in the PR like any catalog change. \
Then delete the runtime queue: ingredient_weights.rs, the weights batches in ingredient_names::work_pass, Estimate.weight_gaps and Weights in nutrition, the load_and_enqueue call in estimate_calories.rs, the weights part of the status and retry API (IngredientWeightsStatus) and of ramekin-ui/src/pages/SettingsPage.tsx, and tests/test_ingredient_weights.py. \
Learned estimates for foods the catalog doesn't know keep their own cup and piece weights. \
Leave the ingredient_weight_estimates table in place (see blocked-calorie-drop-dead-columns). \
Run make pipeline; expect calorie coverage changes in data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md. \
The fill needs an API key (cli.env) and costs one batch of LLM calls.",
